reading: the SAVING column is what the body's reference structure would gain if every run
of length L cost one token instead of 1.535 on average -- an UPPER bound,
because the glyph sequence of a run is fixed by the rule assignment and cannot be chosen
freely per run. The capacity column says whether enough distinct-character tokens exist
at each length for an assignment to aim at, and "CAPACITY BINDS" marks a length where the
body contains more runs than the vocabulary has distinct-char tokens to serve them.
